description:
Update the ProviderFailureTracker::is_valid method in crates/gribtract-fetch/src/probe.rs to call should_reprobe instead of manually checking the failure threshold.

## Current code (lines 368-372)
```rust
for (provider, &count) in &self.consecutive_failures {
    if count >= self.consecutive_failure_threshold {
        return false;
    }
}
```

## Should be
```rust
for provider in self.consecutive_failures.keys() {
    if self.should_reprobe(provider) {
        return false;
    }
}
```

This ensures consistency with the gribtract/src/provider_probe.rs implementation and avoids duplicating logic.

## Acceptance criteria
- ProviderFailureTracker::is_valid calls should_reprobe for each provider
- Code compiles without errors
- Logic is equivalent to current implementation
